{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"30e8e41e5ab44c4e1c92faebc0aa2a6ead56ffc0a63dbf3043d95b85ca2a94ea","digest":{"component_or_area":"CI Module-size gate shell","key_entities":[".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml",".github/workflows/test.yml",".github/module-size-allowlist.txt","listed=$(grep -vE...)","tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py"],"problem_keywords":["module-size gate","allowlist drain","grep exit code","bash pipefail","CI workflow"],"propositions":["The module-size gate shell in both gerrit-verify.yaml and test.yml aborts with exit 1 when the allowlist is empty (no non-comment lines) because grep returns 1 on no-match and pipefail+set -e causes the step to fail before the over-cap check runs","The grep command extracting allow-listed files must be guarded with '|| true' so that a zero-match result does not abort the step under bash -e -o pipefail","The gate must continue to function identically for non-empty allowlists and still fail when non-allow-listed over-cap files are detected","The same one-line fix (guarded grep) must be applied to the identical 'listed=' line in both workflow files"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787540462599000001,"uuid":"a6a23a26-d733-4441-90e1-3de98cbc39a2"}